# #99 round 5, acceptance shape: after a function's plain write to `len`
# the global binding holds a number, so a later builtin-style call dies
# ("cannot call num") on BOTH sides — the self-hosted compiler used to
# fresh-slot the write and happily print 3 (silent acceptance).
define f() as:
    len is 5
    return 0
f of null
print of len
print of (len of [1, 2, 3])
